<speak>We do have separate user spaces now. Before that, the desktop was a mixture of my work files, my wife's recipes, and our daughter's school projects. Nobody dared delete anything because it might belong to somebody else. We finally sat down together and sorted it out. The funny thing is, once we each had a place, there wasn't nearly as much clutter. A lot of it was duplicate copies with slightly different names. I had been saving things again simply because I couldn't find the earlier copy.</speak>